From 5c9e111630e68244092471f207715d727a91d57e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fujii Hironori <fujii@igalia.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:57:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [GTK][WPE] Destroy the renderer of a page suspended for a
 process swap

When a cross-site navigation swaps processes, the previous page is kept in the back/forward cache of its
process (SuspendedPageProxy) for up to 30 minutes. Its drawing area keeps the LayerTreeHost alive: the
compositing thread with its Skia GPU context, the swap chain and the tiles, although the UI process no
longer shows it. If the page is restored, the UI process creates a new drawing area and
WebPage::reinitializeWebPage() replaces the old one, so the old renderer is never used again.

This also happens for the initial about:blank page when the first navigation gets a
Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy browsing context group switch (x.com, youtube.com), which left a second web
process with ~75 MiB of GPU memory.

Destroy the renderer as soon as the page is suspended for the process swap.

